{"title":"1951 AHSME Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Of the following statements, the one that is incorrect is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9ec5188e013ded3a9547240dd8ff0742c689ec9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\text{Doubling the base of a given rectangle doubles the area.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"442\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/7/9174f94e64d7a4e4b6b8bed661bddfdc24751da4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\text{Doubling the altitude of a triangle doubles the area.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"413\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/4/ff4e7e50f5a928be577c40e342378892654b03e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\text{Doubling the radius of a given circle doubles the area.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"427\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/d/6ad410ed77d46fce94aabba3699f7ae2c16024ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\text{Doubling the divisor of a fraction and dividing its numerator by 2 changes the quotient.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"674\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/acc3d12c9af13d26583fca6446c8e4e609837f19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{Doubling a given quantity may make it less than it originally was.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"516\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The well-known area formula for a circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/2/3a29e7889fad76777233bc77041cf045d9fb6f15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = \\pi r^2$\" width=\"63\" height=\"15\" />, so doubling the radius will result it quadrupling the area (since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/7/ae7ee9bb3abe538edfafd8d5cb12217d09502541.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39; = \\pi (2r)^2 = 4 \\pi r^2 = 4A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"202\" height=\"21\" />). Statement <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/f/fffc7368e8e7b77c88b0b4bf732c88c60e27b439.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"30\" /> is therefore incorrect, and is the correct answer choice.\n</p><p><br />\nStatements <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/6/a46f6af01fcf3bb5f6cac2316bc4de9bb3906bec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/1/b7193f66028e13f331d53ff5e6942c4b05587465.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> are evidently correct, since in triangles the area is directly proportional to both the base and the height (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/2/b92a81693dd8ba47c3c6c01b7af011cc514c8dc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = \\frac{1}{2} bh$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"69\" height=\"37\" />). Statement <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/0/b305929a95b53f14a0ad53eba1d8560626e1f28b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> is also correct: let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/a/9da7aefca12d55ec434dcfdb6e5e9bbce2663180.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q = \\frac{a}{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"45\" height=\"33\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/f/d0feed1b90f62684874f9126ebf893bcf79a1a66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q&#39; = \\frac{a \\div 2}{2b} = \\frac{a}{4b} = \\frac{q}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"163\" height=\"37\" />, which is a change from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. Finally, statement <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75e41e3cd48cee2c6866cfbb4386a8e99d3482f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(E)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"18\" /> is true: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/5/4f525a52b1197a53dab56f0570d1dc7974b906c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x &lt; x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"53\" height=\"12\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/a/36a68e8aa6ec6f48231ad80a4851f84bacf641b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, as doubling a negative number makes it even more negative (and therefore less than it originally was).\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME\" title=\"1951 AHSME\">1951 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/